{"schema_version":"1","event_id":"4c3ef04d05824a22b7701ab3a7bd28d6","incident_id":"7384c05795db4f11af30ce2a896bb425","ts":"2026-09-20T07:56:18.743471Z","stage":3,"kind":"triage","actor":"llm","summary":"ambiguous: H_db vs H_meta","payload":{"hypotheses":["H_db","H_meta"],"ambiguous":false,"triage":{"ambiguous":false,"reasoning":"The fingerprint shows a severe incident with a fully saturated DB (pool_busy_ratio=0.96, db.query_p99_ms ~1.5s), maxed retry_ratio (3.8x), and near-total error and timeout rates at all layers. SLO is heavily breached (p99=2.5s >1s). Payments and orders are equally slow, matching DB times. There is no recent deploy (no change_events), and all edges and services are equally affected (no sign of a single bad node, hotkey, or noisy neighbour). These facts simplify candidates to: (1) DB capacity genuinely exceeded (H_db), (2) self-sustaining retry storm (H_meta), or (3) generalized resource excess in an upstream (CPU or queues), but we have direct evidence of DB at near-full capacity. Retry storms could be present as retry_ratio is high, but feedback loop evidence is needed to separate between the two. The proposed experiments (shed, retry cap, failover) are suited to separate these. Capacity excess or dependency limit (H_db) and self-sustaining retries (H_meta) are the most plausible causes.","hypotheses":[{"id":"H_db","label":"Degraded dependency / DB capacity","description":"DB is saturated (pool_busy_ratio near 1, high db.query_p99_ms) at all traffic levels. Orders and payments are equally slow, error rates are high, and all paths show DB latency as the shared bottleneck.","evidence":["db.pool_busy_ratio=0.96 (nearly 100%)","db.query_p99_ms=1493 (high at all qps)","svc.orders.retry_ratio=3.8 (suggests retries are abundant)","svc.gateway.p99_ms and svc.orders.p99_ms both >2s","No change_events, so not a deploy","No localized hotspots, so not hotkey or single node issue"]},{"id":"H_meta","label":"Self-sustaining retry storm","description":"Retry_ratio is very high (3.8+). It's possible the original cause is gone, but excess retries are saturating the dependency. Once the backlog is cleared (e.g. by a retry cap), the system may remain healthy.","evidence":["svc.orders.retry_ratio=3.81 (very high)","db.pool_busy_ratio very high","High error_rate and timeout_rate could sustain ongoing retries"]}],"predictions":[{"hypothesis_id":"H_db","experiment_id":"shed_10_20s","during":[{"metric":"db.pool_busy_ratio","direction":"down"},{"metric":"svc.gateway.p99_ms","direction":"down"},{"metric":"svc.orders.p99_ms","direction":"down"},{"metric":"svc.orders.retry_ratio","direction":"flat"}],"after_release":[{"metric":"db.pool_busy_ratio","direction":"up"},{"metric":"svc.gateway.p99_ms","direction":"up"},{"metric":"svc.orders.p99_ms","direction":"up"},{"metric":"svc.orders.retry_ratio","direction":"flat"}],"confirms_if":{"phase":"during","metric":"svc.gateway.p99_ms","expect":"within_baseline"}},{"hypothesis_id":"H_db","experiment_id":"shed_50_20s","during":[{"metric":"db.pool_busy_ratio","direction":"down"},{"metric":"svc.gateway.p99_ms","direction":"down"},{"metric":"svc.orders.p99_ms","direction":"down"},{"metric":"svc.orders.retry_ratio","direction":"flat"}],"after_release":[{"metric":"db.pool_busy_ratio","direction":"up"},{"metric":"svc.gateway.p99_ms","direction":"up"},{"metric":"svc.orders.p99_ms","direction":"up"},{"metric":"svc.orders.retry_ratio","direction":"flat"}],"confirms_if":{"phase":"during","metric":"svc.gateway.p99_ms","expect":"within_baseline"}},{"hypothesis_id":"H_db","experiment_id":"retry_cap_0_20s","during":[{"metric":"db.pool_busy_ratio","direction":"flat"},{"metric":"svc.gateway.p99_ms","direction":"flat"},{"metric":"svc.orders.retry_ratio","direction":"down"}],"after_release":[{"metric":"db.pool_busy_ratio","direction":"flat"},{"metric":"svc.gateway.p99_ms","direction":"flat"},{"metric":"svc.orders.retry_ratio","direction":"up"}],"confirms_if":null},{"hypothesis_id":"H_db","experiment_id":"db_f